><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20251110095423+10'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20251110095426+10'00'" name="9f76ac6c-5dc8-4898-ac39-ed4c2ef67ae3" page="12" coords="59.981094,385.645142,433.197205,385.645142,59.981094,373.969177,433.197205,373.969177,59.981094,372.604004,433.175720,372.604004,59.981094,360.928040,433.175720,360.928040,59.981094,359.625885,433.196716,359.625885,59.981094,347.949951,433.196716,347.949951,59.981094,346.647766,433.186310,346.647766,59.981094,334.971802,433.186310,334.971802,59.981094,333.669647,433.206970,333.669647,59.981094,321.993713,433.206970,321.993713,59.981094,320.628510,433.123444,320.628510,59.981094,308.952576,433.123444,308.952576,59.981094,307.650391,433.175903,307.650391,59.981094,295.974426,433.175903,295.974426,59.981094,294.672272,433.175232,294.672272,59.981094,282.996338,433.175232,282.996338,59.981094,281.631134,433.144226,281.631134,59.981094,269.955200,433.144226,269.955200,59.970596,268.653015,433.133759,268.653015,59.970596,256.977051,433.133759,256.977051,59.960098,255.674896,433.165100,255.674896,59.960098,243.998947,433.165100,243.998947,59.960098,242.633789,433.144470,242.633789,59.960098,230.957840,433.144470,230.957840,59.960098,229.655670,433.185852,229.655670,59.960098,217.979721,433.185852,217.979721,59.960098,216.677551,417.688416,216.677551,59.960098,205.001602,417.688416,205.001602" rect="59.595215,204.636719,433.571838,386.010010" subject="Comment on Text" title="Alexander Gibson"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: This study researched the plausibility of the use of IMUs for the estimation of applied&#xD;forces for wheelchair racing propulsion. Although perfect agreement was not attained&#xD;between IMU and force plate measurements for mean force, max force and rate of force&#xD;development over a starting motion, sufficient accuracy was obtained, particularly in&#xD;the forwards direction over short periods during acceleration from stationary. In the&#xD;absence of a directly comparable measurement system, promising agreement was&#xD;observed with data presented in the literature. Whilst further research is required to&#xD;differentiate trunk motion from the system dynamics, the potential of IMUs have been&#xD;demonstrated, which can be of large benefit to athletes who are in need of in-field&#xD;testing methodologies having ease of use, applicability and are more financially viable&#xD;than the current gold standard of the SMARTWheel. Reduced accuracy was observed&#xD;for athletes having spoked wheels, suggesting this solution should only be used on&#xD;carbon wheels (either disc or aero spoke). Caution must be used in data interpretation;&#xD;however, data from IMUs can facilitate in-field kinetic assessment of performance.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="12" rect="493.227997,293.645142,677.228027,385.645142"
/></highlight
